# The site's rendered PNGs: the og:image card, the Stripe product image, the touch
# icon and the favicon. `pnpm icons` rewrites every one of them in full whenever the
# mark or the card copy changes, so as ordinary blobs each change adds the whole set
# to history, forever, in every clone. LFS keeps the pointer in git and the bytes out.
#
# There are no app screenshots here yet (Armada has no capture pipeline). When there
# are, add their directory below rather than a second .gitattributes.
#
# They are committed rather than generated at build time so a clone can build the
# site without running `pnpm icons`, which needs the repo-root design/ and a Mac's
# fonts. That is also why any CI job that builds or deploys this site must check out
# with LFS (`lfs: true` on actions/checkout): `release` is `astro build && wrangler
# deploy`, so a checkout without it publishes 130-byte pointer files named .png.
#
# This file lives in apps/website/ rather than at the repo root because its patterns
# are relative to its own directory. Hoisting it up would silently stop matching, and
# the next refresh would commit these as ordinary blobs.
public/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
